{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1222947-saitama-one-punch-character-idea","id":1222947,"title":"Saitama - One Punch - Character Idea","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-29T11:05:37-07:00","id":1222947,"title":"Saitama - One Punch - Character Idea","content":"Edition: Mage The Ascension 2E<br /> <br /> For anyone wondering who Saitama is <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5OIQM608joc\" target=\"_blank\">!SPOILER WARNING! HERE</a> is one of his fights.<br /> <br /> My group tends to be much more fun focused and less setting focused when we play so I wanted to have a good back up character in case mine dies. We have a lot of combat in our game. What kind of magic and stats would work as One Punch Man?<br /> <br /> Edit: I realize that he is an incredibly powerful character and the scale of this fight is not what is in our game. I'm just curious how this would work and thought it would be a very fun character in a combat focused campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24181,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24181-donavan","user":"Donavan","date":". 05-29-2018, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24181-donavan","name":"Donavan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T13:11:07-07:00","id":1222980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Donavan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1222947-saitama-one-punch-character-idea#post1222947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of magic and stats would work as One Punch Man?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's - scarily enough - not many different things that are needed.<br /> <br /> Ingedient 1: Forces 5<br /> Ingredient 2: Time 4<br /> Ingredient 3: Being a Marauder whose twisted, insane paradigm of being 'Just a normal guy, training, really guys' constantly charges a Forces Shield (Damage absorption of various kinds of forces) and Forces-based Strength (So much that everything pretty much dies in one punch and the successes are high enough to cause destruction in the landscape - Forces 5 is excellent at that.) and Time 1 (Sense of excellent timing) and Time 3 (Insane speed) through literally subconcious ritual, hung with Time 4 to be released in an instant.<br /> <br /> ...annnd that's it. You don't even need to be an Akashic, or Do or anything of that fancy stuff. The whole point is, after all, that he's just 'A normal guy being a hero for fun' in his head. Deep Denial, there.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> If you tone things down from Marauderdom (and Saitama's absolute denial), you can build an Akashic who accomplishes such things through a more sane Akashic paradigm, actual rituals of focusing the mind, and - due to Paradox - smaller scale. Note that this 'smaller scale' is still fricking scary with this level of Forces in the character's endgame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-29-2018, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T18:25:44-07:00","id":1223083,"title":"","content":"Dang I do not currently have that much. I only have force 2, time 2, correspondence 2, Arete 4. The best I got now is C2 to perfectly know space around me to reduce dodge difficulty and F2 to increase damage.<br /> <br /> Edit: words are hard <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24181,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24181-donavan","user":"Donavan","date":". 05-29-2018, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24181-donavan","name":"Donavan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T00:10:57-07:00","id":1223129,"title":"","content":"Well, Forces 5 just blows it over the top. One thing that is kind of unique to the Forces sphere is, that while the higher levels (like any other sphere) enable new kinds of effects, the lower levels also increase in potency - with Forces 2 you can telekinetically lift a human. With 5 you can lift....really, really, really big things. But it's the same Forces 2 effect.The same goes for the destructive properties (although damage-wise, the normal table always applies - just not the area).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T06:36:03-07:00","id":1223197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Donavan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1222947-saitama-one-punch-character-idea?p=1223083#post1223083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dang I do not currently have that much. I only have force 2, time 2, correspondence 2, Arete 4. The best I got now is C2 to perfectly know space around me to reduce dodge difficulty and F2 to increase damage.<br /> <br /> Edit: words are hard <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it seems that you will have to do a lot of push-ups, sit-ups, squats and running to get there <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In the meantime, use the same concept, as Ambrosia says. Very simple, very focused, Forces &amp; Time. Coupled with use of Ritual casting (focused trough training) to get extra potent effects.<br /> <br /> A cyborg familiar that absorbs Paradox could help make over the top punches more often...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T06:55:24-07:00","id":1223216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1222947-saitama-one-punch-character-idea?p=1223197#post1223197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A cyborg familiar that absorbs Paradox could help make over the top punches more often...</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha I had a whole response typed up before I realized you were referring to Genos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24181-donavan","name":"Donavan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T18:00:33-07:00","id":1223452,"title":"","content":"A Ritual casted version of 'Hands of Death' From the Guide to the Technocracy should get you the 'one punch' effect. But Saitama level stuff is kind of.... Well best to hope one isn't on earth when you break it out. Or else the Paradox would be unfortunate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T19:20:52-07:00","id":1223482,"title":"","content":"Saitama's probably the hardest character to emulate in OPM because his defining features are simply being &quot;OVERPOWERed' which works wonderfully in OPM because his powers while super don't really help him with his life. I am not sure how you make him differ signficantly from your average combat character while maintaining a sense of balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T02:42:16-07:00","id":1223557,"title":"","content":"The Forces/Time build is probably the best bet (you could probably make a case for some Prime and Life for investing into his suit or reinforcing his own pattern....but that's probably being to complicated where Forces/Time is probably all you need). <br /> <br /> One thing to keep in mind is that Saitama has the power of a Master if not a Arch-Master...but he has the enlightenment/arete about how reality <i>REALLY </i>works of a much, <i>much</i> less enlightened mage. Though if your just aping him rather then porting him, it probably doesn't matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11535-furoan","name":"Furoan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-31T19:47:11-07:00","id":1223815,"title":"","content":"Ya its not so much that I wanted to make him so much as a future character might be very very combat focused. I wanted to see if the one punch abilities could be replicated in mage. Turns out just about any hero, whether anime or comic, can be easily recreated in mage with the right blend of paradigm and spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24181-donavan","name":"Donavan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}